# Point the app at your PC where user_login/server runs (same Wi‑Fi as your phone).
# Use your PC's Wi‑Fi IPv4 from `ipconfig` (ignore VMware/Hyper-V adapters unless you use those for networking).
# Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.192.217.29:4000
# Restart Expo (stop and `npx expo start -c`) after changing.
#
# If the app says it cannot reach the API but the IP is correct:
# 1) On the phone's browser open: http://YOUR_PC_IP:4000/api/health — if it never loads, Windows Firewall is likely blocking port 4000. In an elevated (Run as administrator) PowerShell run:
#    netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="Node API 4000" dir=in action=allow protocol=TCP localport=4000 profile=private,domain
# 2) Ensure user_login server is running and shows "listening on http://0.0.0.0:4000" (LISTEN_HOST=0.0.0.0 in .env).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
